WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Transcriber: Eunice Tan
Reviewer: Tanya Cushman

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:21.300
Well, this is a police officer's uniform -

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.886
a Baltimore City police officer,
in particular, named Robert White.

00:00:25.886 --> 00:00:27.814
He gave me this uniform

00:00:27.814 --> 00:00:31.452
when he and I became
the very best of friends.

00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:33.251
But, you know, I first met Robert -

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:37.523
well, I first heard about Robert White
when I was a teenager,

00:00:38.173 --> 00:00:40.114
and then I later met him.

00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:44.814
I met him just a month
after he got out of prison.

00:00:45.092 --> 00:00:49.093
He was in prison, serving a sentence

00:00:49.093 --> 00:00:54.023
for assault with intent to murder
two black men, with a shotgun,

00:00:54.023 --> 00:00:55.834
and another sentence -

00:00:55.834 --> 00:01:01.442
conspiring to bomb
a synagogue in Baltimore.

00:01:01.442 --> 00:01:04.036
Now, I am a professional musician.

00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:07.852
I tour all over this country
and around the world, playing music.

00:01:07.852 --> 00:01:12.550
So how do I end up
with a policeman's uniform?

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.891
He worked for the police department

00:01:15.891 --> 00:01:17.382
by day.

00:01:17.382 --> 00:01:19.584
But he also had another job,

00:01:19.714 --> 00:01:23.267
which required
a different kind of uniform.

00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:33.118
He was the grand dragon
of the Ku Klux Klan

00:01:33.118 --> 00:01:35.002
for the State of Maryland.

00:01:35.002 --> 00:01:36.855
This is his robe.

00:01:36.855 --> 00:01:38.470
This is what he wore

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.994
when he conspired to bomb the synagogue

00:01:40.994 --> 00:01:45.415
and when he made plans
to kill two black men, with a shotgun.

00:01:51.508 --> 00:01:54.722
To understand why I have these items,

00:01:54.722 --> 00:01:57.610
let's take a little journey
back in my life.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:01.056
I was born in Chicago in 1958.

00:02:01.056 --> 00:02:04.221
At the age of 10, in 1968,

00:02:04.221 --> 00:02:07.425
my parents had moved
to Belmont, Massachusetts -

00:02:07.425 --> 00:02:09.485
a suburb of Boston.

00:02:09.485 --> 00:02:13.745
I was one of two black kids
in the entire area -

00:02:13.745 --> 00:02:15.328
at least in the school.

00:02:15.328 --> 00:02:18.224
I joined the Cub Scouts at the age of 10

00:02:18.224 --> 00:02:22.145
at the invitation of some
of my white, male friends.

00:02:22.145 --> 00:02:26.368
And we had a march
from Lexington to Concord

00:02:26.368 --> 00:02:29.211
to commemorate the ride of Paul Revere.

00:02:29.211 --> 00:02:33.132
My den mother let me carry
the American flag.

00:02:33.132 --> 00:02:36.636
And as I was marching
as the only black scout in this parade,

00:02:36.636 --> 00:02:39.733
along with the Girl Scouts, Boy Scouts,
Cub Scouts, and Brownies -

00:02:39.733 --> 00:02:42.719
I think 4-H Club was there
and some other organizations -

00:02:42.719 --> 00:02:44.822
as I was marching down the street,

00:02:45.422 --> 00:02:47.469
somewhere along the parade route,

00:02:47.469 --> 00:02:49.463
I began getting hit

00:02:49.463 --> 00:02:54.590
with bottles, soda pop cans,
rocks, and debris from the street

00:02:54.590 --> 00:03:00.966
by just a small group of white spectators
mixed in with the all-white crowd

00:03:00.966 --> 00:03:02.554
on the sidewalk.

00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:06.748
This was the first time
I ever experienced anything like this,

00:03:06.748 --> 00:03:08.492
and I did not understand.

00:03:08.492 --> 00:03:12.437
I thought perhaps those people
did not like the Scouts.

00:03:12.437 --> 00:03:15.355
I did not realize
I was the only Scout getting hit

00:03:15.355 --> 00:03:18.846
until my den mother and the other
scout leaders came rushing over

00:03:18.846 --> 00:03:20.800
and huddled over me with their bodies

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.002
and escorted me out of the danger.

00:03:23.622 --> 00:03:26.432
They never explained why,
even though I kept asking,

00:03:26.432 --> 00:03:29.006
"Why are they hitting me?
Why are they hitting me?"

00:03:29.006 --> 00:03:31.580
What had I done wrong?

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.814
When I got home,

00:03:33.814 --> 00:03:36.643
my mother and father,
who were not at the march,

00:03:36.643 --> 00:03:39.815
were fixing me up with Mercurochrome
and Band-Aids and asking me,

00:03:39.815 --> 00:03:42.246
"How did you fall down
and get all scraped up?"

00:03:42.246 --> 00:03:43.869
I told them, "I didn't fall down."

00:03:43.869 --> 00:03:46.921
I told them exactly what happened.

00:03:46.921 --> 00:03:49.397
For the first time in my life,

00:03:49.397 --> 00:03:52.046
my parents sat me down, at the age of 10,

00:03:52.046 --> 00:03:54.474
and explained racism to me.

00:03:54.474 --> 00:03:57.763
I had absolutely no idea
what they were talking about.

00:03:57.763 --> 00:04:00.425
It was inconceivable to me

00:04:00.425 --> 00:04:02.741
that someone who had
never laid eyes on me,

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:04.044
never spoken to me,

00:04:04.044 --> 00:04:06.929
knew absolutely nothing about me

00:04:06.929 --> 00:04:10.759
would want to inflict pain upon me
for no other reason than this:

00:04:10.759 --> 00:04:12.340
the color of my skin.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.780
So I did not believe my parents.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.980
But more and more incidents
began happening,

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.934
and I realized my parents
had told me the truth.

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:23.512
I didn't know why people felt that way,

00:04:23.512 --> 00:04:26.075
but I realized that
there were some people who did.

00:04:26.075 --> 00:04:30.121
So at the age of 10,
I formed a question in my mind.

00:04:30.121 --> 00:04:31.402
That question was

00:04:31.402 --> 00:04:36.284
"How can you hate me
when you don't even know me?"

00:04:37.174 --> 00:04:38.575
So I grew up,

00:04:38.575 --> 00:04:40.226
in my adolescent years,

00:04:40.226 --> 00:04:45.248
spending a lot of time buying books
on black supremacy, white supremacy,

00:04:45.248 --> 00:04:48.129
the Nazis in Germany,
the neo-Nazis over here,

00:04:48.129 --> 00:04:50.514
the Ku Klux Klan, anti-Semitism -

00:04:50.514 --> 00:04:53.555
trying to understand that ideology,

00:04:53.555 --> 00:04:55.710
trying to get the answer to my question:

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.790
"How can you hate me
when you don't even know me?

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.456
None of these books provided the answer.

00:05:01.456 --> 00:05:04.336
So then, in my adult life,

00:05:04.336 --> 00:05:05.996
I thought, you know what?

00:05:05.996 --> 00:05:08.652
Who better to ask

00:05:08.652 --> 00:05:11.468
"How can you hate me
when you don't even know me?"

00:05:11.468 --> 00:05:15.605
than someone who would join
an organization

00:05:16.275 --> 00:05:22.247
whose historical premise has been
hating those who do not look like them

00:05:22.247 --> 00:05:24.728
and who do not believe as they believe.

00:05:24.983 --> 00:05:28.534
So I had my secretary, who books
my bands and all that kind of stuff -

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:31.056
I said, "Listen, I want you
to get a hold of this guy.

00:05:31.056 --> 00:05:32.878
His name is Roger Kelly."

00:05:32.878 --> 00:05:35.174
I acquired Mr. Kelly's phone number.

00:05:35.174 --> 00:05:39.660
Mr. Kelly is what's known
as the imperial wizard.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.411
Bob White was a grand dragon,
meaning state leader.

00:05:42.411 --> 00:05:46.187
Imperial wizard is a national leader
in the Ku Klux Klan.

00:05:46.187 --> 00:05:48.801
I was told, "Do not fool
with Mr. Kelly, Daryl.

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:50.226
He will kill you."

00:05:50.439 --> 00:05:53.167
But I had to have
the answer to my question,

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:56.068
and I was hoping it wouldn't be
the final answer if I met him.

00:05:56.252 --> 00:05:59.589
So I gave Mary his phone number and said,

00:05:59.589 --> 00:06:01.189
"Give him a call.

00:06:01.189 --> 00:06:03.542
Do not tell him that I'm black.

00:06:04.002 --> 00:06:08.232
But see if he'll sit down
and give your boss an interview -

00:06:08.232 --> 00:06:10.916
he wants to discuss the Ku Klux Klan."

00:06:10.915 --> 00:06:11.916
So she did.

00:06:11.916 --> 00:06:13.671
Mr. Kelly agreed.

00:06:13.671 --> 00:06:16.502
So we reserved a motel room.

00:06:16.502 --> 00:06:18.645
Mary and I got there early.

00:06:18.645 --> 00:06:22.757
Right on time, to the minute,
there was a knock on the door.

00:06:22.757 --> 00:06:25.421
Mary hops up and runs
around the corner, opens the door.

00:06:25.421 --> 00:06:29.744
In walks Mr. Kelly and his bodyguard.

00:06:29.744 --> 00:06:33.014
The bodyguard was armed
with a sidearm right here on his hip.

00:06:33.014 --> 00:06:35.452
When they saw me,
they just kind of like froze

00:06:35.452 --> 00:06:37.722
because they were expecting a white guy.

00:06:37.722 --> 00:06:40.748
I stood up and went like this
to show I had nothing in my hands,

00:06:40.748 --> 00:06:41.745
and I approached.

00:06:41.745 --> 00:06:43.752
I said, "Hi, Mr. Kelly, I'm Daryl Davis."

00:06:43.752 --> 00:06:46.064
He shook my hand;
the bodyguard shook my hand.

00:06:46.064 --> 00:06:48.410
I said, "Come on in,
have a seat, have a seat."

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:50.616
Mr. Kelly sat down,

00:06:50.616 --> 00:06:53.572
and the bodyguard
stood at attention to his right.

00:06:53.572 --> 00:06:56.070
And we conversed -

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.906
agreed on some things,
disagreed on other things.

00:06:58.906 --> 00:07:00.700
But he let me know -

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.402
he let me know that I was not his equal.

00:07:05.132 --> 00:07:07.839
I was inferior; he was superior.

00:07:07.839 --> 00:07:13.315
And this was justified and determined
by the color of my skin.

00:07:13.315 --> 00:07:14.649
I wasn't there to fight him;

00:07:14.649 --> 00:07:18.626
I was there to learn from him:
where does this ideology come from?

00:07:18.626 --> 00:07:21.266
Because once you learn
where it comes from,

00:07:21.266 --> 00:07:23.973
you can then try to figure out
how to address it

00:07:23.973 --> 00:07:25.696
and see where it's going.

00:07:25.696 --> 00:07:27.378
So we continued conversing.

00:07:27.378 --> 00:07:31.770
Maybe about a little over an hour
into this interview,

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:35.244
there's kind of a strange noise
in the room, kind of (unidentified sound),

00:07:35.244 --> 00:07:36.744
and we all jumped.

00:07:36.744 --> 00:07:38.462
And I popped up out of my seat.

00:07:38.462 --> 00:07:40.418
There was a table between us,

00:07:40.418 --> 00:07:42.622
and I was ready to come across that table

00:07:42.622 --> 00:07:45.777
and take down Mr. Kelly and the bodyguard

00:07:45.777 --> 00:07:50.143
because I knew that Mr. Kelly
had made that noise.

00:07:50.143 --> 00:07:52.974
I didn't know what that noise was;
I could not discern it.

00:07:52.974 --> 00:07:56.252
I kept hearing the voice of the person
who gave me his number, saying,

00:07:56.252 --> 00:07:59.470
"Daryl, do not fool
with Roger Kelly - he will kill you."

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.283
I did not want to die that day,

00:08:01.283 --> 00:08:03.689
but I knew he'd made the noise,
and I'm thinking,

00:08:03.689 --> 00:08:05.592
"What did I just do, what did I just say

00:08:05.592 --> 00:08:07.953
to cause him to make
some kind of weird noise?"

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:11.085
And, you know, I'd gone
into what you call survival mode.

00:08:11.085 --> 00:08:14.080
In survival mode, people will do
one of three things.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.247
Some people, when you fear for your life -

00:08:16.247 --> 00:08:18.582
some people will just tense up
and start shaking.

00:08:18.582 --> 00:08:22.198
And you can be taking a hammer or a bat
and hitting them on the head,

00:08:22.198 --> 00:08:25.795
and they won't even deflect the blows -
just be mm-mm-mm like this.

00:08:25.795 --> 00:08:30.966
That is called paralysis by fear,
and it is a real thing.

00:08:30.966 --> 00:08:32.440
The second thing people will do

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.310
is they will try to run away
as quickly as possible

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:40.849
to put as much distance between
the source of the fear and themselves.

00:08:40.849 --> 00:08:44.430
That is the best option
if you can do that.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.232
However, it was not an option for me,

00:08:47.232 --> 00:08:51.137
because you cannot outrun
a bullet in a motel room.

00:08:51.137 --> 00:08:53.600
I was not armed,
neither was my secretary.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.741
The only person I know for sure
who was armed was the bodyguard -

00:08:56.741 --> 00:08:58.461
you could see his weapon right here.

00:08:58.461 --> 00:09:01.648
I did not know if Mr. Kelly had a weapon
up under his jacket or not.

00:09:01.648 --> 00:09:04.194
He was wearing a dark blue suit and tie.

00:09:04.684 --> 00:09:10.859
The third option is do a preemptive strike
to mitigate the danger.

00:09:10.859 --> 00:09:13.324
In other words,
get them before they get you.

00:09:13.324 --> 00:09:15.137
So I was about to do that.

00:09:15.137 --> 00:09:19.651
And when I came up out of my seat,
I was looking right into Mr. Kelly's eyes.

00:09:19.651 --> 00:09:23.391
I didn't say a word, but my eyes
were speaking loud and clear.

00:09:23.391 --> 00:09:27.560
In fact, my eyes were shouting so loud,
he could hear my eyes.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.254
My eyes were saying to him,

00:09:29.254 --> 00:09:31.646
"What did you just do?"

00:09:31.646 --> 00:09:34.653
Well, Mr. Kelly's eyes
had fixated upon mine,

00:09:34.653 --> 00:09:38.450
and his eyes were silently asking me
the same question

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.628
while the bodyguard
had his hand on his gun,

00:09:40.628 --> 00:09:43.451
looking back and forth between
the Klan leader and me, like,

00:09:43.451 --> 00:09:46.015
"What did either one of y'all just do?"

00:09:46.015 --> 00:09:49.288
Well, Mary - she realized what happened.

00:09:49.768 --> 00:09:54.417
She had filled the hotel room
ice bucket with ice

00:09:54.417 --> 00:09:57.250
and put some cans of soda
in there to get them cold,

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:00.904
to be hospitable
and offer Mr. Kelly a beverage.

00:10:00.904 --> 00:10:02.965
The ice had melted,

00:10:02.965 --> 00:10:05.707
and the cans came cascading down the ice,

00:10:05.707 --> 00:10:07.603
and then it made that same noise.

00:10:07.603 --> 00:10:13.547
And we all began laughing
at how ignorant we all had been.

00:10:13.547 --> 00:10:17.337
Now, I won't say
this was a learning moment,

00:10:17.337 --> 00:10:19.817
but it was definitely a teaching moment.

00:10:19.817 --> 00:10:21.568
And what was taught was this:

00:10:21.568 --> 00:10:24.150
all because some "foreign" -

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:27.235
and underscore, highlight,
circle the word "foreign" -

00:10:27.235 --> 00:10:29.787
entity of which we were ignorant -

00:10:29.787 --> 00:10:31.862
being the bucket of ice and cans of soda -

00:10:31.862 --> 00:10:37.288
entered into our little comfort zone
via the noise that it made,

00:10:37.288 --> 00:10:41.591
we all became fearful
and accusatory of one another.

00:10:41.591 --> 00:10:45.602
Thus ignorance breeds fear.

00:10:46.252 --> 00:10:49.139
We fear those things we do not understand.

00:10:49.139 --> 00:10:52.592
If we do not keep that fear in check,

00:10:52.592 --> 00:10:55.968
that fear, in turn, will breed hatred

00:10:55.968 --> 00:10:59.087
because we hate those things
that frighten us.

00:10:59.087 --> 00:11:02.037
If we do not keep that hatred in check,

00:11:02.037 --> 00:11:05.717
that hatred, in turn,
will breed destruction.

00:11:05.717 --> 00:11:08.949
We want to destroy
those things that we hate.

00:11:08.949 --> 00:11:11.395
Why? Because they cause us to be afraid.

00:11:11.395 --> 00:11:12.516
But guess what?

00:11:12.516 --> 00:11:15.807
They may have been harmless,
and we were just ignorant.

00:11:15.807 --> 00:11:20.099
We saw the whole chain
almost unravel to completion

00:11:20.099 --> 00:11:24.035
had the bodyguard drawn his gun
and shot namely me or my secretary

00:11:24.035 --> 00:11:27.782
because it's his job to protect his boss
and protect himself

00:11:27.782 --> 00:11:32.714
or had I pounced and hurt one of them,
trying to protect myself or my secretary.

00:11:32.714 --> 00:11:34.574
We did see -

00:11:34.574 --> 00:11:38.633
we did see that whole chain
unravel to completion

00:11:38.884 --> 00:11:44.881
three months ago in Charlottesville,
Virginia, two hours from where I live.

00:11:44.881 --> 00:11:46.934
Because ignorance was present.

00:11:46.934 --> 00:11:48.541
fear was present,

00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:50.291
hatred was present,

00:11:50.291 --> 00:11:52.691
and destruction occurred

00:11:52.691 --> 00:11:57.354
when a white supremacist got in his car
and tried to mow down people

00:11:57.354 --> 00:12:01.650
and resulted in killing one young lady
named Heather Heyer.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:05.169
So we carried on with this interview.

00:12:05.169 --> 00:12:06.957
No more incidents.

00:12:07.937 --> 00:12:10.762
I would invite Mr. Kelly to my home.

00:12:10.762 --> 00:12:11.958
He would come to my home.

00:12:11.958 --> 00:12:13.408
He'd bring his bodyguard,

00:12:13.408 --> 00:12:15.264
who would sit on the couch next to him.

00:12:15.264 --> 00:12:17.168
Sometimes the bodyguard would get bored,

00:12:17.168 --> 00:12:19.368
pull out his gun,
and twirl it around like this

00:12:19.368 --> 00:12:21.427
while Mr. Kelly and I talked.

00:12:21.427 --> 00:12:23.567
I would invite over
some of my other friends -

00:12:23.567 --> 00:12:26.965
my Jewish friends, my black friends,
my white friends, other people -

00:12:26.965 --> 00:12:30.510
just to engage in conversation
with Mr. Kelly.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:33.340
Other than me, I wanted him
to experience different people.

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:34.866
This went on for a couple years.

00:12:34.866 --> 00:12:36.756
He did not invite me to his home,

00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:41.546
but he would have dinner or lunch
at my table with me -

00:12:41.546 --> 00:12:46.040
this inferior person
that he deemed not his equal.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.563
After a couple years,

00:12:47.563 --> 00:12:51.182
he began coming down
to my house by himself -

00:12:51.182 --> 00:12:54.152
a national leader in the Ku Klux Klan.

00:12:54.152 --> 00:12:56.685
And then he began
inviting me to his house.

00:12:56.685 --> 00:12:58.720
I would see his Klan den,

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:03.566
and I would take pictures and take notes
for my own knowledge and things.

00:13:03.566 --> 00:13:06.828
Then he began inviting me to Klan rallies.

00:13:06.828 --> 00:13:11.608
I'd go to these Klan rallies
that have a 20- or 30-foot wooden cross -

00:13:11.608 --> 00:13:15.205
two beams tied together,
wrapped in burlap.

00:13:15.205 --> 00:13:19.119
The burlap was soaked
in what they call "Klan cologne,"

00:13:19.119 --> 00:13:21.863
otherwise known
as diesel fuel or kerosene.

00:13:21.863 --> 00:13:26.181
And Klansmen and Klanswomen
in their robes and hoods and torches

00:13:26.181 --> 00:13:29.672
would parade around
in a circle around the cross,

00:13:29.672 --> 00:13:32.008
and the grand dragon
or imperial wizard would say,

00:13:32.008 --> 00:13:33.276
"Klansmen, halt!"

00:13:33.276 --> 00:13:34.422
And they'd all stop.

00:13:34.422 --> 00:13:36.847
Then he'd say, "For God!"
And they'd say "For God!"

00:13:36.847 --> 00:13:38.639
"For a race!"
"For a race!"

00:13:38.639 --> 00:13:40.615
"For country!"
"For country!"

00:13:40.615 --> 00:13:42.532
"Klansmen, approach the cross!"

00:13:42.532 --> 00:13:45.446
And they'd all close in
to the base of the cross.

00:13:45.446 --> 00:13:47.320
"Klansmen, light the cross!"

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:50.758
And they'd throw their torch
down at the foot and whoosh!

00:13:50.758 --> 00:13:53.160
This big cross would be on fire.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:57.246
There you go - there's one
such rally with a Klansman.

00:13:57.936 --> 00:14:01.016
That's conversing
with the Klan at a rally.

00:14:01.016 --> 00:14:03.527
And there's a rally
with the cross on fire.

00:14:03.527 --> 00:14:06.374
Now, they would give speeches.

00:14:06.374 --> 00:14:10.509
I would take more notes
and try to absorb and try to understand -

00:14:10.509 --> 00:14:13.403
not that I'm believing
in what they're preaching,

00:14:13.403 --> 00:14:18.405
but I'm trying to learn and understand
what is the impetus for it.

00:14:18.405 --> 00:14:21.892
So after a while,

00:14:21.892 --> 00:14:26.970
CNN got wind of this
and wanted to do a story on me.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.260
They knew me as a musician;

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.361
they knew who Mr. Kelly was
as a Klan leader.

00:14:30.361 --> 00:14:33.261
So they followed me to a rally.

00:14:33.261 --> 00:14:36.769
First, they came to my gig on Friday night
to show what I really do.

00:14:36.769 --> 00:14:37.852
Then Saturday morning,

00:14:37.852 --> 00:14:41.074
they followed me to a Klan rally
two hours from my house.

00:14:41.074 --> 00:14:42.076
And they said to me,

00:14:42.076 --> 00:14:44.561
"Do you think Mr. Kelly
will even talk to us?"

00:14:44.561 --> 00:14:46.750
I said, "I will do better than that.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.388
When this rally is over,

00:14:48.388 --> 00:14:51.402
I will get Mr. Kelly,
the imperial wizard of the Klan,

00:14:51.402 --> 00:14:52.405
to come to my house,

00:14:52.405 --> 00:14:55.711
and you can interview the Klan leader
inside a black man's house."

00:14:55.711 --> 00:14:57.360
They said, "Oh, okay."

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.830
(Laughter)

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.326
So they filmed the rally.

00:15:00.326 --> 00:15:01.960
And when the rally was over,

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.616
I spoke with Roger Kelly,
told him what was going on,

00:15:04.616 --> 00:15:05.621
and he agreed.

00:15:05.621 --> 00:15:09.733
He drove, without his bodyguard,
two hours out of his way,

00:15:09.733 --> 00:15:13.341
sat in my basement
and interviewed with CNN.

00:15:13.341 --> 00:15:18.286
And this clip was shown every hour
for 24 hours all over the world.

00:15:18.286 --> 00:15:19.823
I'm going to show it to you now,

00:15:19.823 --> 00:15:23.902
and I want you to pay particular attention
to what Mr. Kelly says.

00:15:23.902 --> 00:15:28.648
He says that even though he and I
would do different things together,

00:15:28.648 --> 00:15:32.169
it did not change his views on the Klan,

00:15:32.169 --> 00:15:36.865
because his views on the Klan
had been cemented in his mind for years.

00:15:36.865 --> 00:15:40.815
Then he goes on to say how he believes
in separation of the races

00:15:40.815 --> 00:15:44.887
because he finds that to be
in the best interests of all races.

00:15:44.887 --> 00:15:49.492
But listen to what he says about respect,
towards the end of the clip.

00:15:49.492 --> 00:15:50.634
Please show the clip.

00:15:50.634 --> 00:15:53.631
(Video) Carl Rochelle: Davis is one
of the few African-Americans

00:15:53.631 --> 00:15:56.113
you will ever find attending a KKK rally.

00:15:56.113 --> 00:15:58.382
More than attending, he is welcome.

00:15:58.382 --> 00:16:00.865
Roger Kelly: I've got more respect
for that black man

00:16:00.865 --> 00:16:02.671
than I do you white niggers out there.

00:16:02.671 --> 00:16:04.211
(Shouting)

00:16:04.211 --> 00:16:06.071
CR: It's been a tough day for the Klan.

00:16:06.071 --> 00:16:07.029
Their Maryland rally

00:16:07.029 --> 00:16:10.983
found many local residents
rejecting the message of white separatism.

00:16:10.983 --> 00:16:13.871
After it's over, Daryl Davis
hangs around backstage

00:16:13.871 --> 00:16:16.766
with his friend, Klan wizard Roger Kelly.

00:16:20.566 --> 00:16:24.064
It's not unusual for blacks
and whites to be friends,

00:16:24.064 --> 00:16:25.061
but it is unusual

00:16:25.061 --> 00:16:29.128
to find a black man and a Klan leader
chatting pleasantly over an orange soda

00:16:29.128 --> 00:16:31.065
after a Klan rally.

00:16:31.065 --> 00:16:34.084
The relationship started
over a book Davis was writing.

00:16:34.084 --> 00:16:36.956
His secretary set up
an interview with Roger Kelly

00:16:36.956 --> 00:16:39.092
but didn't tell him Davis was black.

00:16:39.092 --> 00:16:41.174
They talked, and talked some more -

00:16:41.174 --> 00:16:44.468
Davis learning about the Klan,
Kelly learning about Davis.

00:16:44.468 --> 00:16:47.227
RK: We get to know one another,
and we do different things.

00:16:47.227 --> 00:16:49.189
It hasn't changed my views about the Klan

00:16:49.189 --> 00:16:50.529
because my views on the Klan

00:16:50.529 --> 00:16:53.182
has been pretty much cemented
in my mind for years.

00:16:53.182 --> 00:16:56.548
CR: Kelly and his Klan friends
go to hear Davis and his band.

00:16:56.548 --> 00:16:58.969
(Music)

00:17:02.305 --> 00:17:04.198
And Davis goes to their rallies.

00:17:04.198 --> 00:17:06.284
Daryl Davis: I sat on the front row,

00:17:06.284 --> 00:17:09.590
and I listened to each
of the Klansmen speak.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.131
Some things I agreed with;
other things I did not.

00:17:12.131 --> 00:17:15.853
CR: Davis thinks that his presence
promotes badly needed understanding.

00:17:15.853 --> 00:17:18.516
DD: Hate stems, I believe, from fear -

00:17:19.096 --> 00:17:20.542
a fear of the unknown.

00:17:20.542 --> 00:17:22.777
And I think this is all across the board,

00:17:22.777 --> 00:17:25.344
regardless of whether
it's a Klansman or anything else.

00:17:25.344 --> 00:17:27.532
CR: But he has no illusions
about the Klan.

00:17:27.532 --> 00:17:30.419
If he did, his friend
would be quick to disabuse them.

00:17:30.419 --> 00:17:32.372
RK: I believe in separation of the races.

00:17:32.372 --> 00:17:34.445
That's in the best interest of all races.

00:17:34.445 --> 00:17:35.557
CR: Does he really?

00:17:35.557 --> 00:17:38.488
Or has friendship
transcended the color barrier?

00:17:38.488 --> 00:17:40.793
Listen to Kelly at a Klan rally.

00:17:40.793 --> 00:17:42.703
RK: I'd follow that man to hell and back

00:17:42.703 --> 00:17:46.274
because I believe in what he stands for
and he believes in what I stand for.

00:17:46.274 --> 00:17:47.750
We don't agree with everything,

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.420
but at least he respects me
to sit down and listen to me,

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.760
and I respect him to sit down
and listen to him.

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:53.760
(Shouting)

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:58.041
CR: The strange relationship
of a KKK wizard and his black buddy.

00:17:58.041 --> 00:18:00.283
In Washington, I'm Carl Rochelle.

00:18:00.283 --> 00:18:01.726
CNN, Sunday morning.

00:18:01.726 --> 00:18:04.094
(Onstage) Respect is the key.

00:18:04.094 --> 00:18:06.567
Sitting down and talking -
not necessarily agreeing -

00:18:06.567 --> 00:18:09.648
but respecting each other
to air their points of view.

00:18:09.648 --> 00:18:12.751
Because of that respect
and my willingness to listen

00:18:12.751 --> 00:18:14.786
and his willingness to listen to me,

00:18:14.786 --> 00:18:16.791
he ended up leaving the Klan,

00:18:16.791 --> 00:18:19.162
and there's his robe right there.

00:18:19.162 --> 00:18:20.297
I am a musician,

00:18:20.297 --> 00:18:22.849
not a psychologist or sociologist.

00:18:22.849 --> 00:18:26.405
If I can do that,
anybody in here can do that.

00:18:26.405 --> 00:18:30.400
Take the time to sit down
and talk with your adversaries.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.729
You'll learn something;
they'll learn something.

00:18:32.729 --> 00:18:35.964
When two enemies are talking,
they're not fighting - they're talking.

00:18:35.964 --> 00:18:37.471
It's when the talking ceases

00:18:37.471 --> 00:18:39.569
that the ground
becomes fertile for violence.

00:18:39.569 --> 00:18:41.115
So keep the conversation going.

00:18:41.115 --> 00:18:42.382
Thank you all very much.

00:18:42.382 --> 00:18:44.250
(Applause)

